OL,0,        ECIMSBWebfax 1   F331A1785257280
OL,3,CMums who lost babies tell court of
OL,4,Ctrauma at being given wrong remains
OL,6,FHe had already admitted 30 counts of
OL,7,Ffraud by false representation relating
OL,8,Fto bodies found at the site, and four
OL,9,F"foetus allegations" of fraud, where
OL,10,Fhe presented ashes to women falsely
OL,11,Fsaying that they were "the remains of
OL,12,Ftheir unborn".
OL,14,FBush also pleaded guilty to a further
OL,15,Fcharge of fraud, covering the ashes of
OL,16,F57 people between 2017 and 2024, and
OL,17,Fone of fraudulent trading relating to
OL,18,Ffuneral plans between 2012 and 2024.
